course: dictionary
lesson: 9278
title: One word, three meanings: span
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word span can mean a length of time, a distance from one end to the other, or stretching across something. The words around it show you which one. «The Earth is about 4.54 billion years old, a span so huge that geologists call it deep time.» A span that huge is a length of time, so span here means how long something lasts.
explain: «Orangutans spend almost all their lives in trees; their arm span can be over 2 metres.» Metres measure length, so this span is a distance: from one end of the arms to the other. Ask yourself: is this about time or about distance? The clue tells you.
explain: When span is a verb, it means to stretch across something or last over it. «The bridge spans the river.» Try the swap test: put «stretches across» in place of spans. The bridge stretches across the river, so the meaning fits.
fact: Span can mean how long something lasts, or how far it reaches from one end to the other.
fact: A «life span» is how long a living thing lives.
fact: A «wingspan» is the distance from one wing tip to the other.
fact: A «hand span» is the distance from the tip of your thumb to the tip of your little finger when your hand is spread out.
fact: As a verb, «spans» means stretches across or lasts over: «The bridge spans the river.»
exercise: «The Earth is about 4.54 billion years old, a span so huge that geologists call it deep time.» What does span mean here? | Stretching across something | *A length of time | A small measure of the hand | A distance from one end to the other
exercise: Which measurement is the distance from the tip of your thumb to the tip of your little finger when your hand is spread out? | Attention span | Life span | Wingspan | *Hand span
exercise: «The bridge spans the river.» What does spans mean? | Moves quickly through | Lasts for a very short time | *Stretches across | Shrinks away from
test: «Orangutans spend almost all their lives in trees; their arm span can be over 2 metres.» Is arm span a length of time or a distance? | A length of time | *A distance from one end to the other | A type of animal | A kind of tree
test: «The Goliath birdeater is the heaviest spider in the world, with a leg span like a dinner plate.» What does leg span mean? | How heavy the spider is | *The distance from one leg tip to the other | To stretch across the ground | How long the spider lives
exam: Which sentence uses span to mean a length of time? | *«Geologists call the vast span of Earth's history deep time.» | «The house spider has a leg span of about 7 centimetres.» | «The bridge spans the river.» | «Spick and span» means very clean.
